### Key finding (the reason GREEN didn't land)
The divergence is **primarily ranking, not just rendering**. Probed oracle node dump (`perl -MGraph::Easy` layout): `Bonn(0,2) → train(2,2) → Ulm(4,2)` inline on one row, anon `buy` cross node **below** train `(2,4)`. Gently ranks `Bonn(4,2)` *east* of train, `Ulm(2,4)` below, anon `(0,2)` inline-west — rotated on all three. The merged `Ulm -- car` path consequently skips train's row, triggering the orthogonality error before any Edge::Cell rendering could even run. Fixing this requires a flow/ranking rule change (edge-node chains inline, cross nodes below) before the render work (EDGE_HOR + EDGE_LABEL_CELL, dash continuation with single arrowhead, label above, Scout.pm flag stripping) can produce the pinned bytes.

